    "checkpoint_limitation": "The original authors evaluate all official test labels/images each epoch and report a best epoch; the released feature archives do not prove which checkpoint produced them. Do not claim a fully blind official benchmark. ATM has upstream access to the generic calibration and validation objects; only our downstream ridge excludes them, so this is development evidence. The authors' reconstruction example inserts a learned diffusion prior before rendering. Native unit coordinates and angular distribution require an empirical check before direct reuse.",
    "training": "The authors' reconstruction code uses a 1024-dimensional EEG vector, regression to OpenCLIP ViT-H/14 image features together with contrastive image loss (training alpha 0.90). preprocessing selects laion2b_s32b_b79k. Official test EEG is averaged over repetitions before encoding; our training approximation averages four released single-presentation feature rows per photograph in published order."
